course: dictionary
lesson: 6022
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and medium is one of them. The sentence around it tells you which meaning is right. «In Britain eggs are sorted by weight into small, medium, large and very large.» The list of sizes gives the clue: medium sits in the middle, between small and large.
explain: Medium can also be a noun. An artist's medium is the material she works with, such as paint, clay or pencil. In science, a medium is what something travels through: sound needs a medium such as air or water to move from one place to another.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Ask: what word would fit here? If you can put "middle-sized" in place of medium and the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Medium (adjective) means in the middle in size, amount or level, not big and not small.
fact: A medium (noun) is a way of communicating or showing something, such as television, paint or the internet.
fact: In science, a medium is a material that something travels through. Sound cannot travel through empty space.
fact: A happy medium is a good balance between two extremes, like not too hot and not too cold.
fact: A medium is also a person who claims to talk to the dead, but this meaning is less common in everyday English.
exercise: «In Britain eggs are sorted by weight into small, medium, large and very large.» What does medium mean in this sentence? | The cheapest kind | Cracked or broken | *In the middle in size, between small and large | Very big and heavy
exercise: In science, sound needs a medium to travel. Which of these is a medium that sound can travel through? | Nothing at all | Silence | Empty space | *Air
exercise: An artist asks, «What medium should I use for this painting?» In this sentence, what is a medium? | A way of joining two colours | A person who draws very well | *The material used, such as paint, clay or pencil
test: Pizzas come in small, medium and large. What does medium mean on the menu? | *Middle size | Free of charge | Smallest size | Biggest size
test: The television, newspapers and the internet are often called what? | Ancient | Curt | *The media | Mediums
exam: Which sentence uses medium as an adjective, meaning in the middle in size? | The artist chose her medium carefully | Sound needs a medium to travel | The media reported the news | *He wore a medium-sized T-shirt
